        "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{{x}^{4}-2{x}^{2}-8}{x-2}=$",
        "worked_solution": "Note that plugging in $x=2$ gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ However, we can use L'Hopital's rule to find this limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{{x}^{4}-2{x}^{2}-8}{x-2} & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{[{x}^{4}-2{x}^{2}-8]^{\u2032}}{[x-2]^{\u2032}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{4{x}^{3}-4x}{1} \\\\  & =4(2)^{3}-4(2) \\\\  & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$",
